<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Liberation Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Liberation Army is the armed force of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a>, tracing its origin to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanchang">Nanchang</a> uprising of 1927. Having won the civil war against the Nationalists, it extended the rule of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> in 1949 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and the borderlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a> in 1950 and 1951.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-liberation-army.jpg" alt="People's Liberation Army" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 燃灯 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:China_Emblem_PLA_shaded.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
